# Native Windows checkouts (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true)
# must keep every text file LF: Git Bash runs the extensionless shims in
# bin/windows/, Python helpers stream LF-framed lines to bash, and bash reads
# Markdown, JSON, jq, and TOML files line by line (docs/windows.md).
* text=auto eol=lf
# Bash parses shell scripts with LF line endings on every supported platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Captured terminal fixtures keep their recorded bytes, CRLF included.
tests/fixtures/**/*.vt -text
